{"case_id":"T8036","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","input semantics"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["ProtoConverter::evmVersionMapping","EVMVersion::osaka","EVMVersion::allVersions","EVMVersion::fromString","EVMVersion::name","EVMVersion::isExperimental"],"reason":"S1 adds the selectable EVM configuration `EVMVersion::osaka()` and includes it in `allVersions()`, `fromString()`, and `name()`, but H0's `ProtoConverter::evmVersionMapping` has no `Program::OSAKA` case and can generate only through `Program::PRAGUE`. Thus S1 + H0 cannot exercise the new Osaka configuration through fuzz input. This gap did not exist in S0 because Osaka was not present there, so the commit introduced it.","evidence":["S1 adds `static EVMVersion osaka() { return {Version::Osaka}; }`.","S1 appends `osaka()` to `EVMVersion::allVersions()` and adds `Version::Osaka`/`\"osaka\"` handling.","H0's `ProtoConverter::evmVersionMapping` enumerates versions from `Program::HOMESTEAD` through `Program::PRAGUE` only.","H0 assigns `m_evmVersion = evmVersionMapping(_x.ver())`, making the protobuf version field its configuration-control path."],"recommended_action":"Extend H0's protobuf version domain with `Program::OSAKA` and map it to `EVMVersion::osaka()` in `ProtoConverter::evmVersionMapping`, preserving fuzz-input control over every production EVM version."}
